# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large official raster (418,912,844 B). Not committed: it exceeds any sensible
# git budget and is reproducible. scripts/fetch_and_verify_data.py places it and
# re-verifies its sha256 against the pin in src/gems/spec.py.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/training_features.tif

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bridge transport parts (419 MB once reassembled) and the bridge copies of the
# two small rasters ARE committed to THIS repository. Reason: earlier versions
# of this project fetched them via codeload from a duplicate repository
# (buffedlizard55-lab/GEMSDOE), which created an eligibility-relevant dependency
# on a repo we intend to archive. The parts are sha256-pinned in
# data/bridge/manifest.json (and re-verified in src/gems/spec.py), so hosting a
# first-party copy here is auditable and removes the cross-repo dependency.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (no longer ignored — the pinned parts live in this repo now)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived artifacts: 12,279,160 px x 105 channels x 4 B ~= 4.9 GB + a 12 MB mask.
# Rebuilt in ~15 minutes by scripts/build_features.py (streaming, tile by tile).
# rank_tables.json (13 MB) is derived the same way: scripts/build_rank_tables.py
# rebuilds it from the sha256-pinned rasters in ~2 minutes, and it carries the
# rasters' own hashes, so committing it buys nothing but churn.
# prob_*.f32.npy are the raw probability surfaces saved for the candidate
# writeup (~49 MB each); rebuilt by any build_submission.py --save-prob run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/evidence/features.f32.npy
data/evidence/_invalid_allband.npy

# Python / tooling noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
build/
dist/

# ...but the evidence JSON and the shipped submission file ARE committed: they
# are the audit trail the site renders, and they are small.
!data/evidence/*.json
!downloads/*.tif

# ...except these two: big derived artifacts, rebuilt from the pinned rasters
# (the rule above would re-include them, so they are listed after it).
data/evidence/rank_tables.json
data/evidence/prob_*.f32.npy
